*.log
.DS_Store
.env

# ⚑ witness writes these while a mutation run is in flight. One of them was committed by a
# `git add -A` during a run — a 765-line copy of the assessor, tracked in the repository, which is
# both noise and a large block of duplicate code the rubric would count. Never again by accident.
*.witnessbak

# ⚑ The BASELINE is not an artefact and must be committed. It is the reviewed, signed-off judgement
# that a mutant is genuinely equivalent — the only thing standing between an exemption and an
# excuse. Ignoring it made the gate pass on my machine, where the file exists, and report a survivor
# on the runner, where it never arrived. A verdict that depends on an untracked file is not a
# verdict anybody else can reproduce, which is the whole point of running it somewhere I do not own.
